        "code": "function NameList() {\n    const names = [\"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\"];\n\n    return (\n        <ul>\n            {names.map((name, index) => (\n                // A key is ALWAYS required when mapping!\n                <li key={index}>{name}</li>\n            ))}\n        </ul>\n    );\n}",
        "tip": "You can map directly inside the JSX `{}` block, or you can map the array to a variable above the `return` statement and just insert the variable. Both are extremely common.",
