        "code": "// BEST: Database ID (Stable, unique)\n{posts.map(post => <Post key={post.uuid} data={post} />)}\n\n// BAD: Array Index (Changes if items are re-ordered or deleted)\n{posts.map((post, index) => <Post key={index} data={post} />)}\n\n// TERRIBLE: Random numbers (Changes on every single render!)\n{posts.map(post => <Post key={Math.random()} data={post} />)}",
        "tip": "Using the array `index` is only acceptable if the list is purely static (items are never added, removed, or re-ordered). If the list can change, using `index` will cause subtle, untraceable UI bugs.",
