        "title": "Difference between <div> and Fragment?",
        "category": "React Fundamentals",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "A `<div>` is a real HTML element. When React renders it, the browser creates a DOM node, which affects CSS styling, layout, and takes up memory. \nA `<Fragment>` is purely a React construct. It completely disappears during the rendering phase and leaves zero trace in the actual HTML DOM.",
        "example": "A Fragment is like a ghost wrapper. It satisfies React's internal syntax rules but vanishes when it touches the browser.",
