        "explanation": "`<React.StrictMode>` is a developer tool (a wrapper component) that highlights potential problems in an application. \nIt does not render any visible UI. It enables additional checks and warnings for its descendants. Crucially, **it intentionally double-invokes certain lifecycle methods and Hooks** (like `useEffect` and `useState` initializers) in development mode to help you find subtle side-effect bugs.",
