        "explanation": "Hooks are special functions (introduced in React 16.8) that allow you to 'hook into' React state and lifecycle features entirely from within Functional Components. \nThey completely eliminated the need to write ES6 Class components. They always start with the word `use` (e.g., `useState`, `useEffect`).",
