        "category": "React Hooks",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "`useEffect` is a hook used to perform Side Effects in functional components. \nA 'side effect' is any operation that reaches outside the React component to interact with the world (e.g., fetching data from an API, manually changing the DOM, setting timers/intervals, or subscribing to WebSockets). \nIt runs *after* the component has rendered to the screen.",
