        "title": "Why is useEffect() used?",
        "category": "React Hooks",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "React components must be 'Pure Functions' during the rendering phase. This means given the same props and state, they must predictably return the exact same JSX, without causing external changes. \nIf you initiate a network request or start a timer directly in the main body of the component, it will trigger every single time the component re-renders (which can be dozens of times per second). `useEffect` isolates these unpredictable, external actions, ensuring they only happen at specific, controlled times.",
