        "example": "The store might look like a giant JSON object containing `{ users: [], auth: { loggedIn: true }, cart: { items: 5 } }`.",
        "code": "import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';\n\n// Creating the single centralized store\nconst store = configureStore({\n  reducer: {\n    cart: cartReducer,\n    auth: authReducer\n  }\n});\n\n// Accessing state directly (rarely done in React, usually use useSelector hook)\nconsole.log(store.getState());",
