        "example": "A legacy Redux setup taking 4 files and 100 lines of code can be written in 1 file and 20 lines using RTK.",
        "code": "// Legacy: Hard to read, prone to mutation errors\nfunction reducer(state, action) {\n  switch (action.type) {\n    case 'ADD': return { ...state, items: [...state.items, action.payload] };\n  }\n}\n\n// RTK: Clean, readable, feels like normal JS\nconst slice = createSlice({\n  name: 'cart',\n  initialState: { items: [] },\n  reducers: {\n    add: (state, action) => { state.items.push(action.payload); } // Magic!\n  }\n});",
