        "explanation": "Optimizing a React app involves a combination of reducing re-renders, shrinking bundle sizes, and deferring expensive operations. Key strategies include:\n1. **Memoization:** Using `React.memo`, `useMemo`, and `useCallback` to prevent unnecessary re-renders.\n2. **Code Splitting:** Using `React.lazy` and Suspense to only load JavaScript chunks when a user navigates to that page.\n3. **Virtualization:** Using libraries like `react-window` to only render the exact list items currently visible on the screen.\n4. **State Colocation:** Moving state as close to where it's needed as possible, so changing it doesn't re-render the whole app.\n5. **Image Optimization:** Compressing images and using modern formats (WebP) or relying on Next.js `<Image>` optimization.",
