        "explanation": "`React.lazy()` is a built-in function that lets you render a dynamic import as a regular component. \nIt is the primary tool used in React to achieve Code Splitting. It takes a function that must call a dynamic `import()`. This must return a Promise which resolves to a module with a `default` export containing a React component.",
