        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "`<Suspense>` is a wrapper component that lets you specify a fallback UI (like a loading spinner) to display while the child components inside it are 'waiting' for something asynchronous to finish. \nHistorically, it was only used to wait for `React.lazy` components to download. In modern React (18+), it is also used to wait for asynchronous data fetching (Server Components or specialized fetching libraries).",
