        "category": "Advanced & Modern React",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "Next.js is a powerful React framework built by Vercel. \nWhile React is technically just a UI library, Next.js provides the full architecture needed for production, including Server-Side Rendering (SSR), Static Site Generation (SSG), file-based routing, API endpoints, and aggressive image/font optimization out of the box.",
        "example": "If you build a blog in plain React (CSR), Google sees a blank page. If you build it in Next.js (SSR/SSG), Google sees a fully rendered HTML page instantly.",
        "code": "// Next.js App Router (v13+) introduces Server Components by default\n// app/page.tsx\nexport default async function Home() {\n    // This fetch happens ON THE SERVER. The client never sees the loading state.\n    const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data').then(r => r.json());\n    \n    return <h1>{data.title}</h1>;\n}",
