        "explanation": "A React Portal provides a first-class way to render a component's HTML output into a completely different DOM node that exists outside the DOM hierarchy of the parent component. \nEven though the element is teleported visually in the DOM, it still behaves like a normal React child (meaning Context and Event Bubbling still work perfectly).",
        "example": "Rendering a Modal. You write the Modal component deep inside your `<Dashboard>` code, but the Portal physically injects the Modal's HTML right before the `</body>` tag so it isn't restricted by the `overflow: hidden` or `z-index` of the Dashboard.",
