        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "You use a Portal when a child component needs to visually 'break out' of its parent's container. \nThe most common CSS issues that force the use of Portals are `z-index` (stacking contexts) and `overflow: hidden`. If a parent div has `overflow: hidden`, any tooltip or modal inside it will be visually chopped off at the edges. Portaling the modal to the `<body>` prevents this.",
