        "explanation": "- **Context API:** A built-in React tool for *Dependency Injection*. It is great for passing static or low-frequency updates (theme, user language) down the tree. It is NOT optimized for complex state changes. If a Context value changes, EVERY component consuming it forcefully re-renders.\n- **Redux:** A third-party *State Management Library*. It is highly optimized for complex, high-frequency updates. Components can subscribe to specific slices of the store, ensuring only the exact components that need to update re-render.",
