        "explanation": "React Query (now TanStack Query) is a powerful data-fetching and server-state management library for React. \nIt completely removes the need to use `useEffect` and `useState` for API calls. It handles fetching, caching, synchronizing, background updating, and error handling of server data with zero configuration.",
        "example": "If a user navigates away from a page and comes back, React Query will instantly show the cached data while secretly fetching the newest data in the background to update the UI seamlessly.",
