        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "CSS-in-JS is a styling methodology where CSS is written directly inside JavaScript files using JavaScript syntax, rather than in external `.css` files. \nThis approach solves several classic CSS problems: global scope collisions, dead code elimination, and sharing dynamic variables (like theme colors) between JavaScript state and CSS rules.",
        "example": "Passing a React state boolean directly into a CSS class to dynamically change its color.",
        "code": "// A conceptual example of CSS-in-JS\nconst styles = {\n    button: (isPrimary) => ({\n        backgroundColor: isPrimary ? 'blue' : 'gray',\n        padding: '10px',\n        borderRadius: '5px'\n    })\n};\n\nfunction Btn({ primary }) {\n    return <button style={styles.button(primary)}>Click</button>;\n}",
