        "mistake": "Confusing CSS-in-JS with inline styles (`style={{ color: 'red' }}`). Inline styles don't support pseudo-classes (like `:hover`) or media queries. CSS-in-JS libraries actually generate and inject real CSS `<style>` tags into the document head at runtime.",
        "summary": "A methodology that allows writing CSS directly inside JavaScript files, enabling dynamically styled components based on React props and eliminating global class name collisions."
