        "title": "How do you mock an API call in Jest?",
        "category": "Testing",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "You should never make real network requests during unit tests (they are slow, flaky, and require an active internet connection). \nInstead, you use Jest functions (`jest.mock` or `jest.spyOn`) to intercept the API call and return fake, controlled data.",
