        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "Cypress is a modern, frontend-centric End-to-End (E2E) testing framework. \nUnlike RTL (which uses a simulated, headless DOM), Cypress actually spins up a real instance of Chrome, Edge, or Firefox, opens your application, and programmatically clicks buttons, types text, and navigates exactly like a human user would.",
        "example": "Writing a script that opens `localhost:3000`, clicks the 'Login' button, types a username and password into the form, submits it, and verifies the URL changes to `/dashboard`.",
        "code": "// Cypress Test Syntax\ndescribe('Login Flow', () => {\n  it('successfully logs in', () => {\n    // Navigate to the app\n    cy.visit('/login');\n    \n    // Interact with real elements\n    cy.get('input[name=\"username\"]').type('admin');\n    cy.get('input[name=\"password\"]').type('password123');\n    cy.get('button[type=\"submit\"]').click();\n    \n    // Assert the URL changed\n    cy.url().should('include', '/dashboard');\n    \n    // Assert the UI updated\n    cy.contains('Welcome back, admin').should('be.visible');\n  })\n})",
