        "title": "What is the custom hooks pattern for architecture?",
        "category": "Enterprise Architecture & Best Practices",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "This is the modern replacement for the Container component pattern. \nInstead of creating wrapper components to house logic, you extract all stateful logic (API calls, side effects, complex math) into a pure JavaScript function (a Custom Hook). \nThe React component then just calls the hook and renders the returned data, keeping the component file small and focused purely on UI.",
        "example": "Extracting form validation logic into a `useForm` hook.",
        "code": "// The Logic (Custom Hook)\nfunction useUser(id) {\n    const [user, setUser] = useState(null);\n    useEffect(() => { fetchUser(id).then(setUser) }, [id]);\n    return { user, isLoading: !user };\n}\n\n// The UI (Component)\nfunction UserProfile({ id }) {\n    // Component is incredibly clean!\n    const { user, isLoading } = useUser(id);\n    \n    if (isLoading) return <Loading />;\n    return <h1>{user.name}</h1>;\n}",
        "tip": "Custom hooks are the absolute best way to share non-visual logic between multiple completely different UI components.",
