        "explanation": "RBAC ensures users only see what they are authorized to see (e.g., standard users vs. admins). \nIn React, you implement RBAC by creating a wrapper component that checks the current user's role against a list of allowed roles. If they don't match, the component renders a fallback (like 'Access Denied' or nothing at all).",
