        "explanation": "Internationalization (i18n) is the process of making your app support multiple languages. \nIn React, this is almost always done using the `react-i18next` library. You extract all hardcoded text strings in your app into JSON translation files. In your components, you use a hook to look up the correct string based on the user's selected language.",
