        "explanation": "Standard React forms require creating a state variable for every single input and writing complex `onChange` handlers. This is slow to write and causes massive performance issues (re-rendering the whole form on every keystroke). \nEnterprise apps use **React Hook Form**. It uses uncontrolled components (Refs) under the hood to completely eliminate unnecessary re-renders while providing a beautiful API for validation, error handling, and submission.",
        "example": "Building a 20-field checkout form that validates instantly without lagging.",
