        "category": "Enterprise Architecture & Best Practices",
        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "Yup and Zod are schema validation libraries. \nWhile React Hook Form can do basic validation (`required: true`, `maxLength: 20`), writing complex validation (e.g., 'Password must have 1 number, 1 symbol, and match the Confirm Password field') in JSX gets extremely messy. \nYup/Zod allow you to define a strict, reusable JavaScript schema representing the valid shape of the data. You pass this schema to React Hook Form, and it automatically handles all the complex validation logic.",
        "example": "Validating that an end-date is strictly after a start-date in a booking form.",
