        "language": "jsx",
        "explanation": "TypeScript is a superset of JavaScript that adds static typing. \nIn React, it solves the massive problem of 'prop drilling anxiety'. When passing data down multiple components, developers often forget what properties an object has, leading to `Cannot read properties of undefined` runtime crashes. \nTypeScript catches these errors instantly in your code editor before you even save the file. It provides intelligent autocomplete (IntelliSense) for your React components' props.",
        "example": "If a `<Button>` component strictly requires a `variant` prop of either `'primary'` or `'secondary'`, TS will throw a red squiggly line if a developer tries to pass `'blue'`.",
