        "explanation": "When dealing with DOM events (like clicks or typing in inputs), you must tell TypeScript exactly what type of HTML element triggered the event. \nReact provides specific Event types (like `MouseEvent`, `ChangeEvent`, `FormEvent`) that you combine with HTML element types (like `HTMLInputElement`, `HTMLButtonElement`).",
