        "explanation": "Webpack is a static module bundler for modern JavaScript applications. \nWhen Webpack processes your application, it builds a dependency graph mapping every module your project needs (JS, CSS, images, fonts). It then packages all of these modules into one or more optimized, minified `.js` bundles to be served to the browser.",
